{%- comment -%}
  HOUSE OF AGHA — MOCK CATALOG · the single source of truth for pricing and promotions.

  Nothing here is real. It stands in for Shopify until the store is connected, and it is read by
  BOTH sides so no page can disagree with another:
    · Liquid sections  →  {% capture j %}{% render 'hoa-catalog-data' %}{% endcapture %}{% assign catalog = j | parse_json %}
    · the browser      →  snippets/hoa-catalog-script.liquid embeds this JSON; assets/hoa-commerce.js
                          normalises it (window.HOA) and prices the shop, product page, related
                          products and the bag from it.

  PRODUCT FIELDS (and what Shopify will supply later)
    regularPrice   whole rupees. The "was" price when the product has an offer, otherwise simply
                   the price (Shopify: compare_at_price, else price)
    salePrice      the selling price when there is an offer, else null (Shopify: price)
    isBestSeller   Shopify: a tag / metafield
    rating, reviewCount   Shopify: reviews app or reviews.rating / reviews.rating_count metafields
    inventory      Shopify: variant inventory_quantity
  Derived, never stored (so they cannot drift): hasOffer, discountPercentage, price, savings.
  A product has an offer only when salePrice is set AND lower than regularPrice.

  PROMOTIONS
    settings.quantityTiers     "buy more, save more": tier % applies to individual fragrance units
                               in the bag (Shopify later: automatic discount / Function)
    settings.freeShippingThreshold   the bag's free-shipping progress bar
    coupons                    validated in the bag (Shopify later: discount codes)
    bundles                    discovery-set is a standalone product with its own price; duo and
                               signature add ordinary fragrance units, so the quantity tiers price them
    pairs                      "Pair it with" suggestion per product
  Keep this valid JSON (the Liquid parses it).
{%- endcomment -%}
